{# =========================================================================
   Typesense front-end atom: one facet checkbox
   =========================================================================
   One facet value + count, composed by the facets region. Override it by
   copying this file into your configured front-end templates directory (the
   `facets` region keeps its `#ts-facets` id, so the morph contract is
   unaffected when you only restyle the item).

   Progressive enhancement: the checkbox submits as `facets[]` with no JS and
   carries the Datastar bind + change refetch when present.

   Variables:
   - value:    the facet value
   - count:    the facet count for this value
   - id:       the input id (unique per facet + value)
   - selected: whether this value is in the current selection
   - endpoint: the fragment endpoint for the Datastar refetch
   - theme:    the merged theme config

   Theme keys: `facetItem` (the <li>), `facetLabel` (the <label>),
   `facetCount` (the count span).
   ========================================================================= #}
{%- set theme = theme ?? {} -%}
<li{{ craft.typesense.attr(theme, 'facetItem', 'ts-facets__item') }}>
    <label{{ craft.typesense.attr(theme, 'facetLabel', 'ts-facets__label flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-700') }} for="{{ id }}">
        <input
            type="checkbox"
            id="{{ id }}"
            name="facets[]"
            value="{{ value }}"
            {{ selected ? 'checked' }}
            data-bind:facets
            data-on:change="$page = 1; @get('{{ endpoint }}')"
        >
        <span>{{ value }}</span>
        <span{{ craft.typesense.attr(theme, 'facetCount', 'ts-facets__count text-gray-400') }}>({{ count }})</span>
    </label>
</li>
